Variable resolution
Variables are resolved by scope prefix. Each ${{scope.KEY}} reference targets a specific variable store:







Syntax
Resolves from




${{project.KEY}}
projects/&lt;name&gt;/project.yaml only


${{environment.KEY}}
projects/&lt;name&gt;/environments/&lt;env&gt;.yaml only


${{service.KEY}}
Service-level vars in appbay.yaml or .env only



There is no cascading fallthrough between stores. An undefined reference produces an explicit error naming the scope and key; Appbay never silently substitutes an empty string.






WarningOnly the project store is implemented



The table above is the intended model. Today loadProjectVars reads a single domain: line from $APPBAY_HOME/etc/system.yaml, and nothing reads projects/&lt;name&gt;/project.yaml or environments/&lt;env&gt;.yaml at all. So ${{project.DOMAIN}} is the one reference that resolves; ${{environment.KEY}} and ${{service.KEY}} always fail.
An unresolved reference survives the render as a literal and the deploy then refuses the app, so this fails safe — but plan around it rather than writing references that cannot work.


# In appbay.yaml or .env
DOMAIN: ${{project.DOMAIN}}         # the only scope reference that resolves today

Magic generators
Appbay supports generator expressions that produce values on first evaluation and are then stored for deterministic re-renders:








Generator
Example
Description




${password:N}
${password:16}
Random alphanumeric string of length N


${uuid}
${uuid}
Random UUID v4


${hash}
${hash}
Deterministic hash of project + environment + service + key


${base64:N}
${base64:32}
Random base64 string of N bytes


${timestamp}
${timestamp}
Current timestamp (evaluated at render time, not stored)

Scoped-env trait
Scope: app
The scoped-env trait injects variables from the project/environment scope chain into the app’s environment:
traits:
  - type: scoped-env
    vars:
      DOMAIN: ${{project.DOMAIN}}
      INSTANCE_ID: ${hash}
The scope prefix selects which variable store is consulted. ⚠️ Only project has one: ${{project.DOMAIN}} reads the domain: line from $APPBAY_HOME/etc/system.yaml. The environment and service prefixes parse but resolve against empty maps, so a reference to either always fails — see Scope Model.

Magic generators in scoped-env
Generator expressions can be used as values:
traits:
  - type: scoped-env
    vars:
      SECRET_KEY: ${password:32}
      INSTALL_ID: ${uuid}
      NODE_HASH: ${hash}
      API_TOKEN: ${base64:48}
Generated values are evaluated once and persisted in the state store. Subsequent renders reuse the stored values for deterministic output.

apps

apps.list
List all discovered apps with runtime status.

Type: query
Input: none
Output: App[] where App is { name, project, environment, status, hasAppbayYaml, serviceCount, traits, collections, tags, errors }



apps.get
Get detailed information for a single app. Returns null if not found.

Type: query
Input: { name: string }
Output: AppDetail | null where AppDetail is { name, dir, composePath, project, environment, status, services, hasAppbayYaml, appbayConfig, errors }



apps.create
Scaffold a new app directory with a minimal compose.yaml and appbay.yaml. Fails if the app name already exists.

Type: mutation
Input: { name: string, image?: string, project?: string } (image defaults to "ubuntu:latest", project defaults to "default")
Output: { success: boolean, message: string, name: string }



apps.import
Import an existing compose project directory as an Appbay-managed app. Copies the source directory into $APPBAY_HOME/etc/apps/&lt;name&gt;/ and writes a minimal appbay.yaml if one is absent.

Type: mutation
Input: { name: string, sourcePath: string }
Output: { success: boolean, message: string, name: string }



apps.delete
Delete an app definition directory. Does not remove Docker volumes unless explicitly requested.

Type: mutation
Input: { name: string, keepVolumes?: boolean } (keepVolumes defaults to true)
Output: { success: boolean, message: string }



apps.overlays
Return overlay connection edges across all apps (or filtered to a single app). Each edge represents a conditional compose merge that activates when a peer app is running.

Type: query
Input: { appName?: string } (omit for all apps)
Output: { edges: OverlayEdge[] } where OverlayEdge is { from, to, active, label, effect, reason }



apps.stats
Return live Docker runtime metrics (CPU %, memory MiB, uptime) for a running app.

Type: query
Input: { appName: string }
Output: { cpu: number | null, memMib: number | null, uptime: string | null }



apps.networks
List Docker networks declared in an app’s compose file.

Type: query
Input: { appName: string }
Output: { name: string, external: boolean, driver: string | null }[]



apps.services.list
List services within an app, enriched with live Docker container status.

Type: query
Input: { appName: string }
Output: Service[] where Service is { name, image, ports, status }



apps.config.get
Read a parsed appbay.yaml for an app. Optionally read a single dot-separated key path.

Type: query
Input: { appName: string, key?: string }
Output: { config: AppbayYaml, valid: boolean } (no key) or { value: unknown, key: string, found: boolean } (with key)



apps.config.set
Write a value at a dot-separated key path in appbay.yaml. Creates the file if absent. Validates the result and reports errors but always writes.

Type: mutation
Input: { appName: string, key: string, value: unknown }
Output: { success: boolean, valid: boolean, errors: string[] }



apps.traits.add
Append a trait to an app’s appbay.yaml. Optionally attach at the service level.

Type: mutation
Input: { appName: string, traitType: string, service?: string }
Output: { success: boolean, valid: boolean, errors: string[] }



apps.traits.remove
Remove the first trait of the given type from an app’s appbay.yaml.

Type: mutation
Input: { appName: string, traitType: string, service?: string }
Output: { success: boolean }



apps.logs.follow
Start streaming Docker logs for all running containers in an app. Publishes each line to the app.logs SSE channel. Returns immediately with the container count.

Type: mutation
Input: { appName: string }
Output: { followed: number }
